{#-
  _filters.html.j2: the filter controls (M2-D4; site/CONTRACT.md, "The list page"). Native,
  labelled controls in fieldsets inside <search>, never a <form> (the CSP has form-action
  'none'). Each control's name is its hash key and its value the key's value (CONTRACT
  section 9). The block ships with `hidden`; the script removes it, and 25-filters.css
  reserves its space so that doesn't move the list. Below 60rem everything but search and
  rank sits behind #f-toggle, whose aria-expanded drives the disclosure. On phones (below
  40rem) search, the rank select and #f-toggle share one row: their labels and the line under
  the select are hidden from sight but stay the controls' names and description, and the
  search box shows "Search", the start of its label, as a placeholder (owner's site ruling of
  2026-10-06, mobile_first_screen_two_fonts). The select's label is "Measure" (selector_label,
  2026-10-05). The set follows the
  owner's rulings of 2026-09-30 (data/reviews/site/2026-09-30.toml: monospace_category,
  license_filter, filters_layout): Category's Monospace means every monospaced font, there is
  no Spacing or license-group filter, "No credit required" shows only while some font needs
  credit, and the operating systems are one select. "Nerd Font available" follows the ruling
  of 2026-09-29 (nerd_filter); the rows it keeps carry the tag of the same name (nerd_tag,
  2026-10-05). Sort sits in the list's header (_list.html.j2).

  #mine, "Fonts you have", is the hopper (Milestone 3, slice 1; owner rulings of 2026-10-21
  to 2026-10-23, inventory_on_list_page and inventory_slice_1_defaults): a visitor's list,
  dropped anywhere on the page, chosen or pasted, takes the fonts they have out of every view
  (55-mine.js). None of its controls has a name, so none reaches the address, and its paste
  box asks the browser not to spell-check, autocomplete, correct or capitalise what it holds.
  The paste box and the Show menu have autocomplete="off", so a reload or Back never restores
  what they held (Firefox restores a form control's value on reload, and both engines on
  Back, where the page isn't kept whole).
  "How to make the list" gives each system's command (data.MINE_COMMANDS), with "(not yet
  tested)" where nobody has run it yet (inventory_linux_tested_only). Its words follow the
  ruling site_status_line (2026-09-29): fonts are "left out of the list", never hidden.
-#}
<search id="filters" class="filters" aria-label="Filter fonts" hidden>
<div class="filters-bar">
<label for="f-q" class="visually-hidden-phone">Search fonts</label>
<input id="f-q" name="q" type="search" maxlength="100" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Search">
<label for="f-rank" class="visually-hidden-phone">Measure</label>
<select id="f-rank" name="rank" aria-describedby="f-rank-measures">
{% for view in list.views %}
<option value="{{ view.key }}"{% if loop.first %} selected{% endif %}>{{ view.label }}</option>
{% endfor %}
</select>
<p id="f-rank-measures" class="measures visually-hidden-phone">{{ list.views[0].measures }}</p>
<button type="button" id="f-toggle" class="filters-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="f-more">Filters<span class="filters-count"></span></button>
</div>
<div id="f-more" class="filters-more">
<fieldset id="f-cat" class="pills">
<legend>Category</legend>
<label class="opt"><input type="radio" id="f-cat-all" name="cat" value="" checked> Any</label>
{% for cat in list.categories %}
<label class="opt"><input type="radio" id="f-cat-{{ cat.value }}" name="cat" value="{{ cat.value }}"> {{ cat.label }}</label>
{% endfor %}
</fieldset>
<fieldset id="f-type">
<legend>Features</legend>
<label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" id="f-var" name="var" value="1"> Adjustable weight (variable font)</label>
<label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" id="f-nerd" name="nerd" value="1"> Nerd Font available</label>
<label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" id="f-hide-limited" name="hide" value="limited"> Accented letters</label>
</fieldset>
{% if list.credit_filter %}
<fieldset id="f-license">
<legend>License</legend>
<label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" id="f-hide-attr" name="hide" value="attr"> No credit required</label>
</fieldset>
{% endif %}
<div id="f-system" class="filters-select">
<label for="f-os">Hide fonts that come with</label>
<select id="f-os" name="hide">
<option value="" selected>Nothing</option>
{% for system in list.systems_os %}
<option value="{{ system.value }}">{{ system.label }}</option>
{% endfor %}
</select>
</div>
<fieldset id="mine" class="mine">
<legend>Fonts you have</legend>
<p class="mine-lead">Give this page a list of the fonts on your computer, and those you have are left out of the list. Your list stays in this tab: nothing is sent or saved.</p>
<p class="mine-phone">Make the list on a computer.</p>
<div id="mine-result" class="mine-result" hidden>
<p id="mine-summary" class="mine-summary"></p>
<p id="mine-near" class="mine-more" hidden></p>
<p id="mine-warning" class="mine-more" hidden></p>
<label for="mine-show">Show</label>
<select id="mine-show" autocomplete="off">
<option value="missing" selected>Fonts you don't have</option>
<option value="all">All fonts, yours marked</option>
<option value="only">Only fonts you have</option>
</select>
<button type="button" id="mine-forget">Forget this list</button>
</div>
<p id="mine-busy" class="mine-busy" hidden>Checking your list…</p>
<div id="mine-error" class="mine-error" hidden>
<p id="mine-error-text"></p>
<button type="button" id="mine-retry" hidden>Try again</button>
</div>
<div id="mine-drop" class="mine-drop">
<p>Drop fonts.txt here</p>
<button type="button" id="mine-choose">Choose file</button>
<input type="file" id="mine-file" hidden>
</div>
<label for="mine-paste">Or paste the list</label>
<textarea id="mine-paste" rows="3" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off"></textarea>
<button type="button" id="mine-check">Check</button>
<p id="mine-how" class="mine-how">How to make the list</p>
<div class="mine-oses" role="group" aria-labelledby="mine-how">
{% for cmd in list.mine_commands %}
<details class="mine-os" id="mine-os-{{ cmd.os }}">
<summary>{{ cmd.label }}{% if not cmd.tested %} (not yet tested){% endif %}</summary>
<p>{{ cmd.where }}</p>
<pre class="mine-cmd"><code id="mine-cmd-{{ cmd.os }}">{{ cmd.command }}</code></pre>
<p class="mine-copy-row"><button type="button" class="mine-copy" data-command="mine-cmd-{{ cmd.os }}">Copy<span class="visually-hidden"> the {{ cmd.label }} command</span></button> <span class="mine-copied" hidden></span></p>
<p>{{ cmd.after }}</p>
</details>
{% endfor %}
</div>
</fieldset>
<button type="button" id="f-clear">Clear filters</button>
</div>
</search>
